#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "490982ac-6197-58eb-8d94-2ef28d659d50" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Function Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0edbbb3-17c4-5d0b-a48b-68844c346709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/ba965b75553f65311903910e182eac9c7b49e4acdf28f79db8712a113051c464.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298577} {:answer/id #uuid "15b81cd2-f3a9-53fe-88b6-0e050a5f3671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9ca3a2fd93541dd1865f95beb53cddeb3ff1e7759e1534ae547c4b943931d24e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298578} {:answer/id #uuid "03fcc353-76f1-5f88-8100-9387e9cf3c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/058a4ec5eba7a1ada3fc5b89ada73819672a19f88fbf4450d1b2c04a4b0db498.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298579} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad8d738-e5d8-5d51-af4e-94f25146333f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/e4fb6cb6b35a80a392e6f5091fddb7c136996927ea1810f0dd1db5d0e263996c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298580} {:answer/id #uuid "3f524f2e-c6d2-577e-b04d-69e261f5737c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/29cf79e3f216a3b33656473fd98bd04252e2abd6304fdd575ee56cd33e1f4c3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15b81cd2-f3a9-53fe-88b6-0e050a5f3671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9ca3a2fd93541dd1865f95beb53cddeb3ff1e7759e1534ae547c4b943931d24e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298578} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd1b1b30-be86-549e-8bd6-7d48f80d867c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ff2f67ba-aacd-54bc-bbee-1f4a1b88dea9" :question/math-academy-id "q-121252" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)=-3xy.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\ge 0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-3x$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/3cfdf7d548c430f225a78fa6c4d915d69207f0a1c090d13cdd530c90865731ef.png)"}]}
